● R's rules confirmed. The margin rule that reproduces all seven cases: a factor
  component of a term gets full indicator coding iff the term with that
  component removed isn't already in the model — with the absent intercept
  satisfiable only once. Let me look at how predict() already models
  factor-bearing interactions, to reuse its conventions:
  Ran 2 shell commands (ctrl+o to expand)

