      585 +/* -----------------------------------------------------------
          +----------------                                              
      586 + * Design-matrix construction, shared by lm() and glm().      
      587 + *                                                            
      588 + * A model term is a set of variables: "wt" is one, "wt:hp" is
          + two, and a                                                   
      589 + * variable holding strings is a factor that expands to indica
          +tor columns. The                                              
      590 + * question each factor raises is whether to emit a column for
          + every level or to                                            
      591 + * drop the first as a reference, and R answers it with the ma
          +rgin rule:                                                    
      592 + *                                                            
      593 + *   The factor f inside term T is coded by contrasts -- refer
          +ence level dropped                                            
      594 + *   -- when T with f removed is itself a term of the model, a
          +nd by full                                                    
      595 + *   indicators when it is not. The empty margin, which is wha
          +t a main effect                                               
      596 + *   reduces to once its own variable is removed, counts as pr
          +esent whenever the                                            
      597 + *   model has an intercept. Without an intercept it counts as
          + present only                                                 
      598 + *   after the first factor main effect has consumed it.      
      599 + *                                                            
      600 + * That one rule reproduces R everywhere:                     
      601 + *                                                            
      602 + *   y ~ g          g's margin is empty and the intercept supp
          +lies it, so g is                                              
      603 + *                  coded by contrasts: gb, gc.               
      604 + *   y ~ g - 1      nothing supplies the empty margin, so g is
          + coded in full:                                               
      605 + *                  ga, gb, gc. This is the case that used to 
          +lose a level and                                              
      606 + *                  fit a model forcing the reference group's 
          +fitted values to 0.                                           
      607 + *   y ~ a + b - 1  a consumes the empty margin and is coded i
          +n full; b then                                                
      608 + *                  finds it present and is coded by contrasts
          +. Coding both in                                              
      609 + *                  full would be rank deficient.             
      610 + *   y ~ a * b      both main effects are present, so both com
          +ponents of a:b are                                            
      611 + *                  coded by contrasts: aB:bY.                
      612 + *   y ~ a:b        neither main effect is present, so both co
          +mponents are coded                                            
      613 + *                  in full and the term spans the whole cross
          +-classification.                                              
      614 + *                                                            
      615 + * Terms are ordered by degree first, as R's terms() does, so 
          +that a margin is                                              
      616 + * always decided against terms that precede it.              
      617 + * -----------------------------------------------------------
          +-------------- */                                             
