● Found the real cause. The IRLS start mu = y + 0.1 makes the initial deviance
  ~0.016, so the first genuine step raises it to 1.54 — and glm's step-halving
  guard treats any deviance increase as divergence and halves the step, up to 10
  times. That's why it needs 7 iterations instead of 4. R only halves when the
  deviance is non-finite:

