      5966 +- **The negative-binomial theta alternation stopped early and
           + started from the                                            
      5967 +  wrong place.** `MASS::glm.nb` does not simply maximise over
           + theta; it alternates                                        
      5968 +  between an IRLS fit at the current theta and a fresh ML est
           +imate of theta at the                                        
      5969 +  current fitted means, and which fit it lands on depends on 
           +the schedule. Four                                           
      5970 +  details of that schedule were wrong here, and all four are 
           +now reproduced:                                              
      5971 +                                                             
      5972 +  - The alternation stopped on a relative test of the log-lik
           +elihood alone,                                               
      5973 +    `|dll| < 1e-7 * (|ll| + 0.1)`. `glm.nb` requires         
      5974 +    `(|dLm| / d1 + |dtheta|) < 1e-8` with `d1 = sqrt(2 * max(
           +1, df.residual))`                                            
